WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.970
In 2023, Northern Africa withdrew 101
per cent of its available fresh water.

2
00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:09.310
Oceania withdrew 3 per cent.

3
00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:14.370
Worldwide, farming takes 72 per
cent of freshwater withdrawals,

4
00:00:14.420 --> 00:00:16.210
mostly for irrigation.

5
00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:21.510
Now, the beef on your plate:
about 15,400 litres per kilogram,

6
00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:23.170
on a world average.

7
00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:25.870
Chicken: 4,300.

8
00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:28.610
So is beef draining the world's rivers?

9
00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:32.570
Is that water pumped from
rivers, or drunk by the cattle?

10
00:00:32.620 --> 00:00:37.110
In this mission, you'll map water stress
and follow virtual water as it travels

11
00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:38.870
the world in trade.

12
00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:41.650
Then you'll calculate the
water in a cotton T-shirt,

13
00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:44.690
and weigh how far to trust one number.

14
00:00:44.740 --> 00:00:48.670
Your mission: decide whether beef
is draining the world's rivers,

15
00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:50.050
and explain why.
